From 72639a34d591468bbb41a2d018a9cf1023c2a583 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:49:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Reuse exact binding derivations in origin projection

Origin projection and observation refresh repeatedly decode and validate the
same bounded binding JSON even when fresh SQL returns identical bytes. Keep
bounded exact-text decode and digest memos, returning caller-owned mappings.
Hashing remains at its former consumer boundary; oversized and nontext values
follow the literal path. No task projection, owner freshness, active stream,
alias resolution or terminal deadline is cached.

Proof: canonical direct-ledger importer suite: 41 files, 775 tests pass.
Expanded binding and accounting suites: 9 tests pass. Original work-count test
fails against parent source. Mutants removing nested copying, digest reuse,
and ensure_boards accounting fail behaviorally. Full scripts/check passes.
Captured-input diagnostic improves .1404-.1572s to .1264-.1437s; unpaired,
plain SQLite openers and frozen clock, NOT live CPU-budget acceptance.

This is one structural optimization for t_09269f57c7cf61e6, not completion of
its under-0.5%-of-a-core Mac acceptance. No live Mac changes were made.
